  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-20T17:31:40.695Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've noticed that several avatars simply break in various ways when various safety settings, particularly shaders, are off.\nWhile this can be handled to a limited extent by properly setting up the fallback shader, this doesn't work in all applications.\nIt would be nice if, much like defining Quest avatars, if we could upload a \"default shader variant\" version of the avatar. A good example is how my avatar uses a shader that has z-offset for overlapping faces. Regardless of what fallback shader is used, none of the available ones have any support for z-offset manipulation, so I'd like to just drag the faces forwards just a tiny bit.\nFor other avatars this would let them tweak the materials to look better with default shaders, much like quest users can.",
